  "body": "Improve ServerNoticeServlet\r\nhttps://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/33a02f0f52a5cd793c0d123463d8a7a1e3f4f198/synapse/rest/admin/server_notice_servlet.py#L28\r\n\r\n> We chatted a bit about this in [#synapse-dev:matrix.org](https://matrix.to/#/!XaqDhxuTIlvldquJaV:matrix.org/$Uc5-_9Ws8gfpQl2zSsJAAqcxugfV3C3ozOrTVKohkEs?via=matrix.org&via=vector.modular.im&via=envs.net) and realize that this is highlighting a bug in the servlet!\r\n> \r\n> * The `txn_id` should be passed into `send_notice` method and then passed through into `create_and_send_nonmember_event` (see `RoomSendEventRestServlet` for the proper way to do this).\r\n>\r\n> It was also pointed out that some more magic might be needed to avoid creating duplicate server-notice rooms too, but maybe we can leave that to a follow-up and just add a note about it.\r\n\r\n_Originally posted by @clokep in https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/pull/9520#discussion_r586435068_\r\n\r\nAlso unit tests are missing.",
